    "explanation": "Rider R-3368 booked TRP-04004 on an upfront quote of SGD 17.90 and was charged SGD 24.40 after the fare was re-rated because of a route change; driver D-4102 drove it. The rider is billed SGD 6.50 over the quote, and that whole amount is returned.\n\nThe route deviation is established on this trip's own trace (EV-GPS-04004, weight 1.0): the trace measures 16.32 km against the booked optimal of 12.10 km (EV-TRIP-04004, weight 1.0), an excess of 4.22 km or 34.88%, which clears both POL-RD-01 gates of 0.8 km and 20% (the trace figure governs, not the rounded trip-record copy). It is not a MATERIAL deviation, being under 8.0 km and under 50%, so POL-RD-06's driver-conduct check is not engaged on materiality, and no repeat pattern exists in any event: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 280 completed trips in 90 days (EV-DPROF-04004). The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags was mentioned only to be set aside; it is context-only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used against the driver.\n\nThe money is decided by the fare model. This is an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip (EV-FARE-04004, fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 17.90), so POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02's distance-and-time recomputation does not run; a detour costs the rider nothing on those lines. Under POL-RD-11(a) the rider is refunded the amount by which the charged total exceeds the quote plus the pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09. Those lines are all zero: erp_total 0.00 (the ledger carries no gantry lines, tolls_erp 0.00), airport_surcharge 0.00 (the trip ends in Pasir Ris, it does not originate at an airport) and waiting_time_fee 0.00. The refund is 24.40 - 17.90 - 0.00 = 6.50, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05, which is 6.50. That is the entire contested amount, so the ruling is FULL_REFUND.\n\nThe driver's statement that he 'just followed the navigation' cites no evidence and no clause, and no traffic advisory covers this trip window: EV-ADVIS-04004-01 is present only as a minted identifier with status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue MISSING_ARTIFACT (disclosed). Under POL-RD-13 the traffic excuse therefore carries no weight, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the deviation stands at the measured figure. Because the driver named no advisory ID of his own, the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle rather than a POL-RD-10(5) contradiction, so the case is decided with money rather than escalated. The chat log (EV-CHAT-04004) holds only pickup logistics with no waypoint_hint, so no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04 excludes any distance, and no amendment or pooled baseline (POL-RD-05, POL-RD-12) supplies a different optimal.\n\nNo POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; the trace is unimpaired (164 fixes, 10-second cadence, maximum gap 10 seconds, largest step 150.1 m); the timestamps are causally ordered; the refund is far below both the SGD 150.00 ceiling and the charged total; and every charge line reconciles to the trace and rate card. No billing-integrity or conduct referral is produced by any clause. The refund of SGD 6.50 does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically."
