    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this was an upfront-quoted trip. The app quoted S$17.90 at booking [EV-TRIP-04004] and the fare ledger shows S$24.40 was charged [EV-FARE-04004]. The ride did run long — the GPS trace measures 16.32 km against the platform's booked optimal of 12.1 km, an excess of 4.22 km or 34.88% [EV-GPS-04004, EV-TRIP-04004] — and that is a deviation ESTABLISHED under POL-RD-01, since both the 0.8 km and 20% limbs pass. But because fare_model is UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd 17.90, POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02 does not run: distance and time were fixed at booking, so no distance-or-time recomputation is available and the rider cannot recover the charged total of 24.40 on those lines. The rider's only remedy is POL-RD-11(a): the amount by which charged_total exceeds the quote plus properly chargeable pass-through lines. Charged total 24.40 − quoted fare 17.90 = 6.50; every properly chargeable line is zero (ERP 0.00, airport surcharge 0.00 because this trip ends in Pasir Ris and does not originate at an airport, waiting-time fee 0.00), so the refund is S$6.50 [EV-FARE-04004]. The whole contested amount of S$6.50 is returned, so this is a FULL_REFUND and the rider is made whole. On the arguments, both sides' central claims are accepted and they converge. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 164 fixes at a 10 s cadence, max gap 10 s, largest consecutive step 150.1 m — none of limbs (a)–(c) fire, so no POL-RD-07(ii) corroboration is needed and POL-RD-10(3) does not hold the case back. The driver's assertion that he 'just followed the navigation' and that the app calculates the fare names no artifact and no clause; under POL-RD-08 such a general assertion carries no weight and no exculpatory clause is available — POL-RD-03 fails because the only traffic advisory for this trip is absent (EV-ADVIS-04004-01, status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT; it is cited for its absence alone and